\h 1 Peter
\toc1 1 Peter
\toc2 1 Peter
\toc3 1PE
\mt1 1 Peter
\c 1
\s1 A Greeting from Peter
\r (\ref 2 Peter 1:1–2|2PE 1:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 1 Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ,
\p To \add the\add* elect who are exiles of \add the\add* Dispersion \add throughout\add* Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia, \add chosen\add*\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Literally \fqa To the elect sojourners of the Diaspora of Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia\ft . These provinces were located in what is now Turkey.\f* \v 2 according to \add the\add* foreknowledge of God \add the\add* Father \add and\add* sanctified by \add the\add* Spirit for obedience to Jesus Christ and sprinkling by \add His\add* blood:
\p Grace and peace be yours in abundance.
\s1 A Living Hope
\p \v 3 Blessed \add be\add* the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! By His great mercy \add He\add* has given us new birth\f + \fr 1:3 \ft Or \fqa has caused us to be born again \ft or \fqa has begotten us again\f* into a living hope through \add the\add* resurrection of Jesus Christ from \add the\add* dead, \v 4 \add and\add* into an inheritance \add that is\add* imperishable, undefiled, and unfading, reserved in heaven for you, \v 5 who through faith \add are\add* shielded by God’s power for \add the\add* salvation \add that is\add* ready to be revealed in \add the\add* last time.
\p \v 6 In this you greatly rejoice, though now for a little while you may have had to suffer grief in various trials \v 7 so that the proven character of your faith — more precious than gold, which perishes even though refined by fire — may result in praise, glory, and honor at \add the\add* revelation of Jesus Christ.
\p \v 8 \add Though\add* you have not seen \add Him\add*, you love \add Him\add*; \add and though\add* you do not see \add Him\add* now, you believe in \add Him\add* and rejoice with an inexpressible and glorious joy, \v 9 \add now that\add* you are receiving the goal of your faith, \add the\add* salvation of \add your\add* souls.
\p \v 10 Concerning this salvation, \add the\add* prophets who foretold the grace to come to you searched and investigated carefully, \v 11 trying to determine the time and setting to which the Spirit of Christ in them was pointing when He predicted the sufferings of Christ and the glories to follow.
\p \v 12 It was revealed to \add them\add* that they were not serving themselves, but you, \add when they foretold\add* the things now announced by those who preached the gospel to you by \add the\add* Holy Spirit sent from heaven. \add Even\add* angels long to look into \add these things\add*.
\s1 A Call to Holiness
\r (\ref Hebrews 12:14–17|HEB 12:14-17\ref*)
\p \v 13 Therefore prepare your minds \add for action\add*.\f + \fr 1:13 \ft Literally \fqa Wherefore gird up the loins of your mind\f* Be sober-minded. Set \add your\add* hope fully on the grace to be given you at \add the\add* revelation of Jesus Christ. \v 14 As obedient children, do not conform to the passions of your former ignorance. \v 15 But just as He who called you \add is\add* holy, so be holy in all you do, \v 16 for it is written: “Be holy, because I am holy.”\f + \fr 1:16 \ref Leviticus 11:44–45|LEV 11:44-45\ref*; Leviticus 19:2\f*
\p \v 17 Since you call on \add a\add* Father who judges each one’s work impartially, conduct yourselves in reverent fear during your stay as foreigners. \v 18 \add For\add* you know that it was not with perishable things \add such as\add* silver or gold that you were redeemed from the empty way of life you inherited from your forefathers, \v 19 but with \add the\add* precious blood of Christ, a lamb without blemish \add or\add* spot. \v 20 He was known before \add the\add* foundation of \add the\add* world, but was revealed in the last times for your sake.
\p \v 21 Through Him \add you\add* believe in God, who raised Him from \add the\add* dead and glorified Him; and so your faith and hope are in God.
\s1 The Enduring Word
\r (\ref Isaiah 40:6–8|ISA 40:6-8\ref*)
\p \v 22 \add Since\add* you have purified your souls by obedience to the truth so that you have a genuine love for your brothers, love one another deeply, from a pure heart.\f + \fr 1:22 \ft SBL, NE, and WH \fqa from the heart\f* \v 23 For you have been born again, not of perishable seed, but of imperishable, through \add the\add* living and enduring word of God. \v 24 For,
\b 
\q1 “All flesh \add is\add* like grass,
\q2 and all its glory like \add the\add* flowers of the field;
\q1 the grass withers and the flowers fall,
\q2 \v 25 but the word of \add the\add* Lord stands forever.”\f + \fr 1:25 \ref Isaiah 40:6–8|ISA 40:6-8\ref*\f*
\p And this is the word that was proclaimed to you.
\c 2
\s1 The Living Stone and Chosen People
\r (\ref Isaiah 28:14–22|ISA 28:14-22\ref*; \ref 1 Corinthians 3:10–15|1CO 3:10-15\ref*; \ref Ephesians 2:19–22|EPH 2:19-22\ref*)
\p \v 1 Rid yourselves, therefore, \add of\add* all malice, deceit, hypocrisy, envy, and slander. \v 2 Like newborn babies, crave pure spiritual milk, so that by it you may grow up in \add your\add* salvation, \v 3 now that you have tasted that the Lord \add is\add* good.
\p \v 4 As you come to \add Him\add*, \add the\add* living stone, rejected by men but chosen \add and\add* precious in God’s sight, \v 5 you also, like living stones, are being built into a spiritual house to \add be\add* a holy priesthood, offering spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through Jesus Christ. \v 6 For it stands in Scripture:
\b 
\q1 “See, I lay in Zion a stone,
\q2 a chosen \add and\add* precious cornerstone;
\q1 and the \add one who\add* believes in Him
\q2 will never be put to shame.”\f + \fr 2:6 \ref Isaiah 28:16|ISA 28:16\ref* (see also LXX)\f*
\p \v 7 To you who believe, then, \add this stone\add* is precious. But \add to those who\add* do not believe,
\b 
\q1 “\add The\add* stone the builders rejected
\q2 has become the cornerstone,”\f + \fr 2:7 \ref Psalm 118:22|PSA 118:22\ref*\f*
\p \v 8 and,
\b 
\q1 “A stone of stumbling
\q2 and a rock of offense.”\f + \fr 2:8 \ref Isaiah 8:14|ISA 8:14\ref*\f*
\p \add They\add* stumble \add because\add* they disobey the word— and to \add this\add* they were appointed.
\p \v 9 But you \add are\add* a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people for \add God’s own\add* possession, to proclaim the virtues of Him who called you out of darkness into His marvelous light. \v 10 Once \add you were\add* not a people, but now \add you are the\add* people of God; \add once you\add* had not received mercy, but now you have received mercy.\f + \fr 2:10 \ref Hosea 2:23|HOS 2:23\ref*\f*
\p \v 11 Beloved, I urge \add you\add*, as foreigners and exiles, to abstain from \add the\add* desires of the flesh, which war against \add your\add* soul. \v 12 Conduct yourselves with such honor among the Gentiles that, though they slander you as evildoers, they may see \add your\add* good deeds \add and\add* glorify God on \add the\add* day He visits us.
\s1 Submission to Authorities
\r (\ref Romans 13:1–7|ROM 13:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 13 Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to \add the\add* king as the supreme \add authority\add*, \v 14 or to governors as those sent by him to punish those who do wrong and to praise those who do right. \v 15 For it is God’s will that by doing good you should silence the ignorance of foolish men.
\p \v 16 \add Live\add* in freedom, \add but\add* do not use \add your\add* freedom as a cover-up for evil; \add live\add* as servants of God. \v 17 Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood \add of believers\add*,\f + \fr 2:17 \ft Literally \fqa Love the brotherhood\f* fear God, honor the king.
\p \v 18 Servants, submit yourselves to \add your\add* masters with all respect,\f + \fr 2:18 \ft Or \fqa in all fear\f* not only to those who \add are\add* good and gentle, but even to those who \add are\add* unreasonable. \v 19 For if anyone endures the pain of unjust suffering because he is conscious of God, this is to be commended. \v 20 How is it to your credit if you are beaten for doing wrong and you endure \add it\add*? But if you suffer for doing good \add and\add* you endure \add it\add*, this \add is\add* commendable before God.
\s1 Christ’s Example of Suffering
\r (\ref Isaiah 53:1–8|ISA 53:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 21 For to this you were called, because Christ also suffered for you, leaving you an example, that you should follow in His footsteps:
\b 
\q1 \v 22 “He committed no sin,
\q2 \add and\add* no deceit was found in His mouth.”\f + \fr 2:22 \ref Isaiah 53:9|ISA 53:9\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 23 When they heaped abuse on Him,
\q2 He did not retaliate;
\q1 when He suffered, He made no threats,
\q2 but entrusted Himself to Him who judges justly.
\q1 \v 24 \add He\add* Himself bore our sins\f + \fr 2:24 \ref Isaiah 53:4|ISA 53:4\ref* (see also LXX)\f*
\q2 in His body on the tree,
\q1 so that we might die to sin
\q2 \add and\add* live to righteousness.
\q1 “By \add His\add* stripes you are healed.”\f + \fr 2:24 \ref Isaiah 53:5|ISA 53:5\ref*\f*
\p \v 25 For “you were like sheep going astray,”\f + \fr 2:25 \ref Isaiah 53:6|ISA 53:6\ref*\f* but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls.
\c 3
\s1 Wives and Husbands
\r (\ref Song of Solomon 1:1–17|1:1-17\ref*; \ref Ephesians 5:22–33|EPH 5:22-33\ref*)
\p \v 1 Wives, in the same way, submit yourselves to \add your\add* husbands, so that even if \add they\add* refuse to believe the word, they will be won over without words by the behavior of \add their\add* wives \v 2 when they see your pure \add and\add* reverent demeanor.
\p \v 3 \add Your beauty should\add* not come \add from\add* outward adornment, \add such as\add* braided hair or gold \add jewelry\add* or fine clothes, \v 4 but from the inner disposition of \add your\add* heart, the unfading \add beauty \add* of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is precious in God’s sight. \v 5 For this is how the holy women of the past adorned themselves. They put their hope in God \add and\add* were submissive to \add their\add* husbands, \v 6 just as Sarah obeyed Abraham \add and\add* called him lord. \add And\add* you are \add her\add* children if you do what is right and refuse to give way to fear.
\p \v 7 Husbands, in the same way, treat \add your\add* wives \add with\add* consideration as a delicate vessel, and \add with\add* honor as fellow heirs of \add the\add* gracious gift of life, so that your prayers will not be hindered.
\s1 Turning from Evil
\p \v 8 Finally, all \add of you\add*, \add be\add* like-minded \add and\add* sympathetic, love as brothers, \add be\add* tenderhearted \add and\add* humble. \v 9 Do not repay evil with evil or insult with insult, but with blessing, because to this you were called so that you may inherit a blessing. \v 10 For,
\b 
\q1 “Whoever would love life
\q2 and see good days
\q1 must keep \add his\add* tongue from evil
\q2 and \add his\add* lips \add from\add* deceitful speech.
\q1 \v 11 He must turn from evil and do good;
\q2 he must seek peace and pursue it.
\q1 \v 12 For \add the\add* eyes of \add the\add* Lord \add are\add* on \add the\add* righteous,
\q2 and His ears are inclined to their prayer.
\q1 But \add the\add* face of \add the\add* Lord \add is\add* against
\q2 those who do evil.”\f + \fr 3:12 \ref Psalm 34:12–16|PSA 34:12-16\ref* (see also LXX)\f*
\p \v 13 Who can harm you if you are zealous for what \add is\add* good?
\s1 Suffering for Righteousness
\p \v 14 But even if you should suffer for what is right, \add you are\add* blessed. “Do not fear what they fear; do not be shaken.”\f + \fr 3:14 \ft Or \fqa “Do not fear their threats; do not be shaken.”\ref Isaiah 8:12|ISA 8:12\ref*\f* \v 15 But in your hearts sanctify Christ \add as\add* Lord.\f + \fr 3:15 \ft BYZ and TR \fqa But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts.\ft This sentence may also be included with the quotation from the previous verse; see \ref Isaiah 8:13|ISA 8:13\ref*.\f* Always be prepared to give a defense to everyone who asks you the reason for the hope \add that is\add* in you. But \add respond\add* with gentleness and respect, \v 16 keeping a clear conscience, so that those who slander you may be put to shame by your good behavior in Christ. \v 17 For \add it is\add* better, if \add it is\add* God’s will, to suffer \add for\add* doing good than for doing evil.
\p \v 18 For Christ also suffered\f + \fr 3:18 \ft NE and WH \fqa died\f* for sins once for all, \add the\add* righteous for \add the\add* unrighteous, to bring you to God. He was put to death in \add the\add* body but made alive in \add the\add* Spirit, \v 19 in whom\f + \fr 3:19 \ft Or \fqa in the spirit, \fv 19\fv*in which\f* He also went \add and\add* preached to the spirits in prison \v 20 who disobeyed long ago when God waited patiently in \add the\add* days of Noah \add while the\add* ark was being built.
\p In \add the ark\add* a few \add people\add*, \add only\add* eight souls, were saved through water. \v 21 And \add this water\add* symbolizes \add the\add* baptism \add that\add* now saves you \add also\add* — not the removal of dirt from the body, but \add the\add* pledge of\f + \fr 3:21 \ft Or \fqa appeal for\f* a clear conscience toward God — through \add the\add* resurrection of Jesus Christ, \v 22 who has gone into heaven \add and\add* is at \add the\add* right hand of God, \add with\add* angels, authorities, and powers subject to Him.
\c 4
\s1 Living for God’s Glory
\r (\ref 1 Corinthians 10:23–33|1CO 10:23-33\ref*)
\p \v 1 Therefore, since Christ suffered\f + \fr 4:1 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa for us\ft .\f* in \add His\add* body, arm yourselves with the same resolve, because anyone who has suffered \add in his\add* body is done with sin. \v 2 Consequently, he does not live out \add his\add* remaining time on earth for human passions, but for \add the\add* will of God. \v 3 For \add you have spent\add* enough time in the past carrying out the same desires as the Gentiles: living in debauchery, lust, drunkenness, orgies, carousing, and detestable idolatry.
\p \v 4 Because of this, they consider it strange of you not to plunge with \add them\add* into the same flood of reckless indiscretion, \add and\add* they heap abuse on you. \v 5 \add But they\add* will have to give an account to Him who is ready to judge \add the\add* living and \add the\add* dead. \v 6 That is why the gospel was preached even to \add those who are now\add* dead,\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Or \fqa to those who are dead\f* so that they might be judged as men in \add the\add* flesh, but live according to God in \add the\add* spirit.
\p \v 7 The end of all \add things\add* is near. Therefore be clear-minded and sober, so that you can pray. \v 8 Above all, love one another deeply, because love covers over a multitude of sins.\f + \fr 4:8 \ft See \ref Proverbs 10:12|PRO 10:12\ref*\f* \v 9 Show hospitality to one another without complaining.
\p \v 10 As good stewards of \add the\add* manifold grace of God, each \add of you should use\add* whatever gift he has received to serve one another. \v 11 If anyone speaks, \add he should speak\add* as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, \add he should serve\add* with \add the\add* strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever \add and\add* ever. Amen.
\s1 Suffering as Christians
\p \v 12 Beloved, \add do\add* not be surprised at the fiery trial that has come upon you, as though something strange were happening to you. \v 13 But rejoice that you share in the sufferings of Christ, so that you may be overjoyed at the revelation of His glory.
\p \v 14 If you are insulted for \add the\add* name of Christ, \add you are\add* blessed, because the Spirit of glory and of God rests on you.\f + \fr 4:14 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa On their part He is spoken of as evil, but on your part He is glorified.\f* \v 15 Indeed, \add none\add* of you should suffer as a murderer or thief or wrongdoer, or even as a meddler. \v 16 But if \add you suffer\add* as a Christian, do not be ashamed, but glorify God \add that you bear\add* that name.\f + \fr 4:16 \ft Literally \fqa glorify God in that name\ft ; NA \fqa glorify God in this matter\f* \v 17 For \add it is\add* time \add for\add* judgment to begin with the family of God; and if it begins with us, what \add will\add* the outcome \add be\add* for those who disobey the gospel of God? \v 18 And,
\b 
\q1 “If it is hard for the righteous to be saved,
\q2 what will become of the ungodly and \add the\add* sinner?”\f + \fr 4:18 \ref Proverbs 11:31|PRO 11:31\ref* (see also LXX)\f*
\p \v 19 So then, those who suffer according to God’s will should entrust their souls to \add their\add* faithful Creator and continue to do good.
\c 5
\s1 Instructions to Elders
\r (\ref 1 Timothy 3:1–7|1TI 3:1-7\ref*; \ref Titus 1:5–9|TIT 1:5-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \add As\add* a fellow elder, a witness of Christ’s sufferings, and a partaker of the glory to be revealed, I appeal to \add the\add* elders\f + \fr 5:1 \ft SBL, NE, and WH \fqa I appeal therefore to the elders\f* among you: \v 2 Be shepherds of God’s flock \add that is\add* among you, watching over them\f + \fr 5:2 \ft NE and WH do not include \fqa watching over them\ft .\f* not out of compulsion, but willingly, as God would have you;\f + \fr 5:2 \ft WH, BYZ, and TR \fqa but willingly\f* not out of greed, but out of eagerness; \v 3 not lording it over those entrusted to you, but being examples to the flock. \v 4 And \add when\add* the Chief Shepherd appears, you will receive the crown of glory that will never fade away.
\s1 Cast Your Cares on Him
\p \v 5 Young men, in the same way, submit yourselves to \add your\add* elders. And all \add of you\add*, clothe yourselves with humility toward one another, because,
\b 
\q1 “God opposes \add the\add* proud,
\q2 but gives grace to \add the\add* humble.”\f + \fr 5:5 \ref Proverbs 3:34|PRO 3:34\ref* (see also LXX)\f*
\p \v 6 Humble yourselves, therefore, under God’s mighty hand, so that in \add due\add* time He may exalt you. \v 7 Cast all your anxiety on Him, because He cares for you.
\p \v 8 Be sober-minded \add and\add* alert. Your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion, seeking \add someone\add* to devour. \v 9 Resist \add him\add*, \add standing\add* firm in \add your\add* faith \add and\add* in the knowledge that your brothers throughout the world are undergoing the same kinds of suffering.
\s1 Benediction and Farewell
\p \v 10 And \add after you\add* have suffered for a little while, the God of all grace, who has called you to His eternal glory in Christ,\f + \fr 5:10 \ft BYZ and TR \fqa in Christ Jesus\f* will Himself restore \add you\add*, secure \add you\add*, strengthen \add you\add*, \add and\add* establish \add you\add*. \v 11 To Him \add be\add* the power forever \add and\add* ever. Amen.
\p \v 12 Through Silvanus,\f + \fr 5:12 \ft That is, Silas\f* \add whom\add* I regard as a faithful brother, I have written to you briefly, encouraging \add you\add* and testifying \add that\add* this is \add the\add* true grace of God. Stand firm in \add it\add*.
\p \v 13 \add The church\add* in Babylon,\f + \fr 5:13 \ft Literally \fqa She in Babylon\f* chosen together with \add you\add*, sends you greetings, \add as does\add* my son Mark.
\p \v 14 Greet one another with a kiss of love.
\p Peace to all of you who \add are\add* in Christ.\f + \fr 5:14 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa Amen.\f*
